The description is of a robe with a deep back opening closed by a hook and loop tab. That sounds like a hospital gown or examination gown, or possibly a bathrobe. It does not say what the robe is made of or who it is for, so the classification is a best guess.

A robe with a back opening could be a patient gown, which would be classified under 6211.43 (women's other garments of man-made fibers) or 6210. Bathrobes fall under 6208.91 (women's) or 6207.91 (men's). The deep back opening and the weak construction suggest a disposable or hospital-type gown, but the phrase "robe" points to a bathrobe or dressing gown. I'm choosing women's bathrobes of cotton: 6208.91.3010 is "women's or girls' bathrobes, dressing gowns... of cotton", or at least that is how I recall it. Alternatively, 6208.92.0010 covers man-made fibers. A knit-versus-woven question also arises, since the 6108 headings cover knit nightwear. I'm going with woven cotton 6208.91.

